From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:17:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: Keep the GPIO domain powered for wake on
 every SoC

Buttons and the PMU line wake the system through the AP GPIO controller.
If PMGR powers its domain off in suspend-to-idle no wake interrupt arrives.
T8010 keeps it on; do the same on S5L8960X, T7000, T7001, S8000/S8003, S8001,
T8011 and T8015. Tested only on T8010.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
